{"tool_name":"rapidopgs","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:rapidopgs"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rapidopgs","home":"https://github.com/GRealesM/RapidoPGS","summary":"A rapid polygenic score calculator for summary GWAS data without validation dataset.\n\nPolygenic scores (PGS) aim to predict complex traits at an individual level based on genetic data. Computation of PGS is based on simply ascertained genome-wide association summary statistics but typically requires an independent test dataset to tune PGS parameters, and for the more sophisticated methods, the computation of LD matrices. Internally tuned methods have recently been proposed that obviate the need for a test dataset, but they remain computationally intensive to run. Here we present R\u00e1pidoPGS, a flexible and fast method to compute PGS without the need to compute LD-matrices, requiring only summary-level GWAS datasets. Based on fine-mapping principles, R\u00e1pidoPGS computes the posterior probability that each variant is causal, which in turn is used to shrink effect sizes adaptively as a function of LD and strength of association","addition_date":"2021-01-18T10:02:44Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:28:56.505675Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:rapidopgs","credit":[{"email":"cew54@cam.ac.uk","name":"Chris Wallace","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Collapsing methods","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3791"},{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"},{"term":"Validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2428"}]}],"name":"RapidoPGS","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab456","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1101/2020.07.24.220392","type":["Preprint"]}],"topic":[{"term":"GWAS study","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3517"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Statistics and probabil